    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0282" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/603–604.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-11-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1081.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the department’s cable
                    November 6, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d205-f1"/> in which was embodied a
                    memorandum to be communicated to the foreign office in reply to their memorandum
                    of the 20th ultimo,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d205-f2"/> I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith a copy of the memorandum in question, which was forwarded to Sir Edward
                    Grey on the 9th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d205-a1.xml" xpointer="d205-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
